te ticket creation age.\n52: - Ticket [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) was submitted on **2026-09-06T14:31:00Z** (12 days post-rollout).\n53: - Ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) was imported on **2026-09-07T18:00:00Z** (13 days post-rollout), with `submitted_at: null` (**unknown date preserved**).\n54: Both tickets postdate the deployment of [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md).\n55: \n56: ### B. Bug 1: URL Expiration Before Export Completion (Takes Too Long / Link Expired)\n57: - **Support Ticket:** [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json)  \n58:   - *Customer report:* Workspace [`record-e733dfbdc6`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json), CSV format, ~1,800,000 estimated rows.  \n59:   - *Symptom:* *\"The download spins for twenty minutes, then the link is expired. We need the full ledger, not the first part.\"*\n60: - **Corroborating Evidence:** [`record-eb2ad86fcb`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)  \n61:   - *Observation Date:* 2026-08-31T15:00:00Z on action [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md).\n62:   - *Metrics:* `expected_rows`: 1,800,000; `worker_output_rows`: 1,800,000; `worker_complete_seconds`: 1,184s (~19.7 minutes).\n63:   - *Root Cause:* `url_ttl_seconds`: 900s (15 minutes), while `signed_url_age_seconds` at worker finish was 1,185s.\n64:   - *Result:* Download failed with HTTP 403. The worker completed 100% of the rows, but because the signed URL was generated at job creation with a 15-minute TTL, it expired ~4.7 minutes before the job finished.\n65: \n66: ### C. Bug 2: Silent Record Omission via Cursor Checkpoint Resumes (Missing Rows)\n67: - **Support Ticket:** [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json)  \n68:   - *Customer report:* Workspace [`record-c81238c2b3`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json), NDJSON format, ~2,100,000 estimated rows. Submitted 2026-09-06T14:31:00Z.  \n69:   - *Symptom:* *\"The file completed but our import saw fewer records than the count on screen.\"*\n70: - **Corroborating Evidence:** [`record-6a8741fe3b`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json)  \n71:   - *Observation Date:* 2026-09-06T14:10:00Z on action [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md).\n72:   - *Metrics:* `expected_rows`: 2,100,000; `worker_complete_seconds`: 844s; `download_status`: 200; `worker_output_rows`: 2,039,441 (deficit of **60,559 rows**).\n73:   - *Root Cause Warning:* `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`.\n74:   - *Result:* When an account relation scan experiences a checkpoint resume, cursor offset handling drops rows, silently exporting an incomplete dataset with a success status (HTTP 200).\n75: \n76: ### D. Why Earlier Smoke Tests and Dashboards Masked These Defects\n77: 1. **Under-scaled Pre-release Validation:** The delivery smoke check for [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md) tested only 50,000 rows. At 50,000 rows, jobs finish well under the 900-second TTL and rarely trigger worker checkpointing.\n78: 2. **False Reassurance from Scope-Restricted Audit:** Evidence record [`record-d46f9580f1`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md) (dated 2026-09-07) corrected the missing-row dashboard to show 100% parity, but explicitly noted:\n79:    > *\"Corrects the record-7c21733985 missing-row dashboard for US CSV jobs under 100,000 rows... The review excludes NDJSON, record-6a8741fe3b, EU workspaces, and URL-expiry failures.\"*\n80:    The dashboard's reported 100% parity applies strictly to small US CSV jobs under 100k rows and deliberately excluded the exact conditions causing the customer failures.\n81: \n82: ---\n83: \n84: ## 4. Next Useful Action\n85: \n86: Within standing authority ([/workspace/product/brief.md](file:///workspace/product/brief.md)), we must prepare reversible changes within this product and guide ticket handling without initiating live external operations:\n87: \n88: 1. **Keep Tickets Open & Update Escalation State:**\n89:    - Retain [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) in an active status. Do not close them as legacy/pre-rollout.\n90:    - Record in product tracking that the issues are valid, reproducible post-rollout defects affecting large workspaces (>1M rows).\n91: \n92: 2. **Prepare Fix for Signed URL Lifecycle (Job-Completion URL Generation):**\n93:    - *Change:* Modify the worker flow in [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md) so signed download URLs are not generated at initial job creation timestamp.\n94:    - *Design:* Either (a) generate the signed URL only once the worker successfully writes and closes the export archive, or (b) implement an endpoint that issues a fresh 15-minute signed URL on demand when the customer clicks \"Download\" in the UI after job completion. This resolves HTTP 403 timeouts regardless of worker duration.\n95: \n96: 3. **Prepare Fix for Cursor Checkpoint Resumption (Missing Rows):**\n97:    - *Change:* Audit the account relation scan cursor serialization and resumption logic within the background worker.\n98:    - *Design:* Ensure boundary cursor offsets are inclusive or properly track composite keys during checkpoint restart so that interruption/resumption does not skip records (addressing the 60,559-row loss observed in [`record-6a8741fe3b`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json)).\n99: \n100: 4. **Establish Large-Scale Verification Fixtures (1M+ and 2M+ rows):**\n101:    - Add integration fixtures matching real enterprise scales (1.8M CSV and 2.1M NDJSON rows).\n102:    - Add automated failure injection to test checkpoint resumption and verify 100% parity against source database rows.\n103: \n104: ---\n105: \n106: ## 5. Important Uncertainty\n107: \n108: 1. **Submission Date of Ticket [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json):**\n109:    - The ticket was imported on `2026-09-07T18:00:00Z`, but its `submitted_at` timestamp is `null` (unknown). Although the matching operational incident ([`record-eb2ad86fcb`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json)) occurred on `2026-08-31T15:00:00Z`, the exact time the customer submitted their ticket cannot be established from this snapshot and must not be invented.\n110: 2. **Format Scope of Cursor Resumption Defect:**\n111:    - The missing-row warning was recorded for NDJSON in [`record-6a8741fe3b`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json). It is currently uncertain whether the cursor checkpoint dropping rows is isolated to the NDJSON serializer or exists in the shared database cursor pagination layer across all formats.\n112: 3. **EU Workspaces Reliability and Compliance:**\n113:    - Per [`record-d46f9580f1`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md), EU workspaces were explicitly excluded from the 2026-09-07 missing-row audit. Their large-scale export failure rate and cursor stability remain unverified in the current evidence.\n114: 4. **Behavior at Higher Scales (>2.1M rows):**\n115:    - The observed failures occurred at 1.8M and 2.1M rows. Workspaces exceeding these volumes may encounter additional unobserved resource limits (e.g. disk spool exhaustion or global worker timeouts).\n116: 5. **Snapshot Boundary:**\n117:    - This analysis is strictly confined to the local snapshot as of `2026-09-08`/`2026-09-09`. Live production telemetry, external database connections, and customer communications are not accessible in this environment.\n118: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":103,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-09T15:12:50Z","content":"The dated recommendation for the export feedback follow-through has been documented in [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings & Decision\n\n* **Do Not Close the Support Tickets:** Tickets [`record-f10fee8e5d`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (submitted date unknown, imported 2026-09-07T18:00:00Z) and [`record-339725ec76`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) (submitted 2026-09-06T14:31:00Z) do not predate the rollout. The `\"age_days\": 14` field in [`record-b851997b7c.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/support/record-b851997b7c.json) represents days elapsed since the August 25 rollout of [`record-7c21733985`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md), not ticket age.\n* **Corroborated Root Causes on Large Workspaces (>1M rows):**\n  1. **Premature Signed URL Expiry (\"takes too long / link expired\"):** Corroborated by [`record-eb2ad86fcb.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-eb2ad86fcb.json) (1.8M CSV rows). The background worker successfully wrote all 1,800,000 rows in 1,184 seconds (~19.7 min), but because signed URLs are generated at job start with a 900-second (15-minute) TTL, download attempts fail with HTTP 403.\n  2. **Silent Record Drop on Checkpoint Resumption (\"missing rows\"):** Corroborated by [`record-6a8741fe3b.json`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-6a8741fe3b.json) (2.1M NDJSON rows). The export finished with HTTP 200 but dropped 60,559 records due to a cursor offset omission flagged by `\"account relation scan resumed after cursor checkpoint\"`.\n  3. **Why Earlier Audits Missed This:** The rollout smoke check ([`record-7c21733985.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/actions/record-7c21733985.md)) only validated 50,000 rows, and the 100% parity dashboard audit ([`record-d46f9580f1.md`](file:///workspace/product/history/evidence/record-d46f9580f1.md)) explicitly excluded NDJSON, large workspaces, EU workspaces, and URL-expiry failures.\n* **Next Useful Actions:** Prepare reversible changes within the product to defer signed URL minting until worker completion (or generate fresh URLs on demand) and correct the account relation scan cursor checkpoint resume logic, accompanied by new 1M+ and 2M+ row verification fixtures.\n\nPlease review [`/workspace/work/decision.md`](file:///workspace/work/decision.md) for the complete analysis, citation of source paths and IDs, and documented uncertainties.","thinking":"**Reviewing export feedback instructions**\n\nReviewing the initial instructions confirms the focus: address support reports of incomplete or slow ledger exports. The objective is to evaluate previous actions and determine the best path forward.\nThe specified workspace and starting files are confirmed.\nThe attached source archive requires reading.\n\n\n"}
